I've just been (re)reading the Elric books, and something drew
itself to my attention.  It seems that Stormbringer is much less
effective against mindless beasts than against intelligent ones.
For those of you with the books, check out "The Pearl at the Heart
of the World", where Elric fights the flame-beetles.  Moorcook notes
that "Stormbringer drew scant energy from such beasts" (I can't
remember if that's the exact quote, but something to that effect...)
Compare that with the effect Stormbringer has on intelligent foes -
the effect is usually fairly instantaneous destruction.

So, how about altering the nethack version of Stormbringer to make
it drain levels proportional to the intelligence of the opponent?  As
it stands, it's not as powerful as it should be - this is a legendary 
runeblade, remember.  It should slay humanoids (even tough ones) in at
most 2 or 3 blows.  Balance this by making it only occasionally drain
levels from dumb creatures like insects.

Opinions?

